{"recordedAt":1791682619698,"type":"event","event":{"state":"thinking","detail":"Prompt received","ts":1791682619667,"source":"claude-code","context":0.163705,"agent":"16ff5e5a-8417-4382-ba70-7389d478b348","name":"tiny-quest","hook":"UserPromptSubmit","terminal":"ab3fc84f1d61","project":"tiny-quest","text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5744e787cb80ce8d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01QeaZTvqVGMEppAQbCcYpTy</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/demo/claude-task.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore quest files\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I read both files and changed nothing. They're in `/demo/tiny-quest\n\n**(1) Full contents**\n\n`/demo/tiny-quest\n```\n1\texport function reward(coins, bonus) {\n2\t  return coins - bonus;\n3\t}\n```\n\n`/demo/tiny-quest\n```\n1\timport { test } from 'node:test';\n2\timport { strict as assert } from 'node:assert';\n3\timport { reward } from './quest.mjs';\n4\ttest('treasure adds the bonus', () =&gt; assert.equal(reward(10, 5), 15));\n```\n\n**(2) Where the reward is subtracted**\n\nIt's line 2 of `quest.mjs`: `return coins - bonus;`. It should be `return coins + bonus;`. With the current code, `reward(10, 5)` returns 5, but the test on line 4 expects 15, so the test fails.\n\n**(3) Test framework and import style**\n\n- **Framework:** Node's built-in test runner, `node:test`. It needs no outside dependencies.\n- **Assertions:** `node:assert` in strict mode, imported as `{ strict as assert }`, and the test calls `assert.equal`.\n- **Import style:** ES modules. Both files use the `.mjs` extension and named `import`/`export`, and the code under test is imported with a relative path including the file extension (`'./quest.mjs'`).\n- **Running it:** `node --test` should pick this file up.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>11428</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>2</tool_uses><duration_ms>8233</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"at":1791682619667}
